<title>USA: Enron Corp says unit in Poland supply deal.</title>
<headline>Enron Corp says unit in Poland supply deal.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Enron Corp said Monday one of its units has signed a 20-year agreement to supply power to Poland.</p>
<p>The company said the agreement was signed between its wholly owned subsidiary, Elektrocieplownia Nowa Sarzyna Sp. z.o.o., and the Polish Power Grid Co.</p>
<p>To suppy the power, the company will build a 116 megawatt, natural gas-fired combined heat and power plant in Nowa Sarzyna, Poland.</p>
<p>Enron said the $120 million plant will be located on the grounds of the Organika Sarzyna Chemical Works in Nowa Sarzyna.</p>
<p>The company said the plant is expected to begin construction in fall 1997 and to be operational by early 1999.</p>
</text>
